
## Outbound HTTP

`GET /upstream` calls `UPSTREAM_URL` (default: this service's own `/hello`) with the client configured by `[http_client]` in `alloy.toml`: explicit connect and request timeouts, no redirects, and no automatic retries. Trace context goes only to hosts listed in `http_client.propagate_trace_context_to`, which is empty, and credentials and cookies are never added.

```bash
UPSTREAM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/hello cargo run
curl -s localhost:8080/upstream
```
